- FAB_MUT and FAB_BIRTH_JITTER;
- noise and liar areas;
- any self-regulated noise controller.

What is missing:
- No experiment separates the belief's four forms.
- The decisive reading, generalisation to a perturbation family NOT trained on, has never been taken.
- The literature predicts the verdict flips with the regime: noise costs in single-pass training and helps with repeated data (replay after training). So constant noise levers are the wrong shape.
- The best-evidenced form, variable mappings (a 'dynamic meaning' area), has no generator. DATA's synthetic source is order-2 Markov only.

new_decisions.options:
(a) Adopt noise defaults on the strength of the belief.
(b) Keep the defaults and never test.
(c) A pre-registered ladder, the 'U-series'.
  - Families:
    - (a) segmentation;
    - (b) LM dropout;
    - (c) tag drop;
    - (d) codec drift;
    - (e) dynamic mapping;
    - (f) liar and noise share;
    - (g) corrupted targets.
  - Design: levels 0 / low / mid / high; 5 paired seeds; matched on tokens and compute; both single-pass and replay regimes.
  - Readings:
    - R1: clean held-out;
    - R2: held-out under the same family;
    - R3: held-out under a family left out of training;
    - R4: forgetting, stability gap and plasticity;
    - R5: in-context adaptation.
  - Plus an ADR-style self-regulated arm.

