conflicts.description:
E4 turns tags ON only if the UNTAGGED mean is not worse than never-tagged. On the toy it is +0.051 worse (t 2.56), so the rule says OFF.
That rule reads only the untagged use case and ignores B's retention. d2's forget_tag.py, re-run here, gives easy-area forgetting from the P2 end to the end of the run:
- tag present at read: +0.31 / +0.29 / +0.28 at drop 0.25, and +0.15 / +0.25 / +0.19 at drop 0;
- never-tagged model: +1.87 / +1.65 / +1.23;
- hard area unchanged (+0.50 / +0.53 / +0.39 vs +0.45 / +0.59 / +0.43).
A tag at the input cut the faded easy area's forgetting about fivefold at 3 of 3 seeds, but only when the tag is present at read time.

The digest, repeated in NEW-12, says tag dropout 0.25 gives an untagged read of 1.32-1.66 against 2.06-2.25 without it. That compares forget_easy at drop 0.25 with untagged mean6 at drop 0.
Verified in d2/out, untagged mean6 compared like for like:
- drop 0.25: 1.736 / 1.757 / 1.670;
- drop 0: 2.246 / 2.214 / 2.064;
- never tagged: 1.751 / 1.665 / 1.621.
Same-family invariance is supported: dropout makes the tagged model usable untagged. There is no gain in clean generalisation over a never-tagged model. That is the falsification pattern of the belief's strong form, for family (c), at toy scale.

Deployment input is the belief's canonical 'unreliable system', but every in-tree reading cuts against tolerance by exposure:
- learning-progress focus drew the liar more than the credible source at 4 of 5 seeds;
- credibility did not emerge untagged;
- majority-false inverted trust at 3 of 3;
- pure-add (the harsh condition) gave +0.444 against +0.046 rehearsed, with no emergent protection;
- WORLD's unanchored 'skip' forecast diverged (latent_std 0.13-0.85, +0.358 at one seed).
The literature agrees: about 250 documents backdoor a model, and label-noise damage is quadratic in the noise rate.

The live, drifting codec was argued partly from the belief. The tree does not support it:
- live vs frozen: caption worse at 11 of 16, understanding worse at 5 of 8, a consistent codec-ceiling cost at 7 of 8;
- coordinate rows are MORE sensitive to code perturbation at 3 of 3.

